; firms.vla - the firms: the Firms sheet, the four answers to the Series 777's last
; question, ungraded, "Which best describes you?", each the style of the firm it founds
; and the name it gives the firm (docs/OMAKASE.md, GUARD.1 and BACK.2). Words alone: one
; macro named after this file, whose body is one call of the library's strings. The
; source includes this file after its manifest, with every other include, and calls
; (firms) where the sheet's rows belong. The exam shows the first four rows' styles as
; the question's options, a row's place its letter; the certificate prints the name of
; the one chosen, and the Overview the name and the style. A name is fictional: one
; that points at a living company or a real mark is marked (check) beside its row and
; gets a reader's glance before it ships (CONTRIBUTING.md). To add a row, read README.md
; beside this file.

(defmacro (firms)
  "the firms: the Firms sheet, a firm a row, its style the exam's last question's option and its name"
  (strings "Firms"                  ; the sheet, hidden among the tabs
    ("Style" 40                     ; its fields, each its header and its width in characters: the style, as a candidate describes it,
     "Name" 30)                     ;   and the firm's name, which the style gives it
    ; each row: the style in the candidate's own words, then the firm's name
    ("I read the prospectus" "Prudent & Sons")
    ("I read the headlines" "Above the Fold Capital")
    ("I read the room" "Read-the-Room Partners")
    ("I feel the market" "Vibes LLC")
    ))                              ; the sheet's end: a firm added goes above this line
